---
import { contactEmail } from '@/components/site/links'

import './privacy.css'

const mailto = `mailto:${contactEmail}`
---

<article class="privacy-policy">
	<p>
		Skin Groove LLC (“Skin Groove”, “we”, “us”) is a virtual esthetics practice
		based in Pennsylvania. This policy explains what information we collect, why
		we collect it, who helps us handle it, and the choices you have. It covers
		this website, our booking and intake forms, our consultations, and our shop.
	</p>
	<p>
		Questions? Email <a href={mailto}>{contactEmail}</a>.
	</p>

	<h2>What we collect</h2>
	<h3>When you book</h3>
	<p>
		Cal.com runs our booking. It collects your name, email address, phone
		number, and appointment details. Stripe processes payment through Cal.com.
		We never see your full card number.
	</p>
	<h3>When you fill in the intake form</h3>
	<p>
		Tally runs our intake form. The form asks for your name, date of birth,
		email address, and location, and how you heard about us. It asks about your
		skin concerns, skin history, diagnosed skin conditions, medications,
		allergies, pregnancy, current routine, past treatments, and habits such as
		sun exposure and sleep. It asks for photos of your skin. It also records
		your consents, your photo sharing choice, and your signature. Most of this
		information is consumer health data. Our
		<a href="/health-data">consumer health data privacy policy</a> explains how
		we treat it.
	</p>
	<h3>When you shop</h3>
	<p>
		Shopify runs our shop and checkout. It collects your name, contact details,
		shipping address, and order details. Shopify processes payment. We never see
		your full card number.
	</p>
	<h3>When you email or text us</h3>
	<p>
		We keep the messages and photos that you send to us, and our replies. Sammy
		texts with clients between consultations, for example for acne check-ins.
	</p>
	<h3>When you visit this website</h3>
	<p>
		This website uses no analytics, no advertising pixels, and no session
		recording. It sets no cookies of its own. When you open the booking or
		intake form, Cal.com or Tally can set the cookies that their service needs
		to work.
	</p>

	<h2>How we use your information</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>To schedule, prepare for, and hold your consultations.</li>
		<li>To give you skincare guidance and product recommendations.</li>
		<li>To take payment.</li>
		<li>To fill and ship your shop orders.</li>
		<li>To answer your messages.</li>
		<li>To keep business records that the law requires.</li>
	</ul>
	<p>
		We do not use your information for advertising. The one exception is a photo
		that you give us separate permission to use in our marketing. We do not sell
		your information.
	</p>

	<h2>Consumer health data</h2>
	<p>
		Your intake answers and skin photos are consumer health data. A booking for
		a consultation can be consumer health data too. Our
		<a href="/health-data">consumer health data privacy policy</a> explains what
		we collect, why, who receives it, and how to use your rights to see, delete,
		or withdraw consent for it.
	</p>

	<h2>How long we keep it</h2>
	<ul>
		<li>
			Intake submissions and photos, and the email copies that Tally sends us:
			we keep them until you ask us to delete them.
		</li>
		<li>
			Photos that you allow us to use in marketing: we keep those photos, and
			your permission, while we use them. If you withdraw your permission, we
			stop new uses and remove the posts and pages that we control. We cannot
			recall emails that we already sent.
		</li>
		<li>
			Booking, payment, and order records: we keep them as long as tax and
			business laws require.
		</li>
		<li>
			Emails and text messages: we keep them while they are useful to your care,
			or until you ask us to delete them.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Service providers</h2>
	<p>These companies help us run Skin Groove:</p>
	<ul>
		<li>Cal.com, for booking.</li>
		<li>Stripe, for consultation payments.</li>
		<li>Tally, for intake forms.</li>
		<li>Shopify, for the shop and checkout.</li>
		<li>Google Workspace, for email and calendar.</li>
		<li>
			Cloudflare, which hosts this website. It processes standard request data,
			such as IP addresses, to deliver pages and to block attacks.
		</li>
	</ul>

	<h2>Security</h2>
	<p>
		Our service providers encrypt your data in transit and at rest. Only Skin
		Groove staff can open intake submissions, and each account uses two-factor
		login. No method of storage is perfectly secure, but we protect your data
		with care.
	</p>
	<p>
		Text messages are less private than our forms, because phone carriers carry
		them. Please do not text us about an urgent medical concern.
	</p>

	<h2>Age</h2>
	<p>
		Our services are for clients 13 or older. A client under 18 needs consent
		from a parent or legal guardian, who completes part of the intake form with
		them. A parent or guardian can ask to see or delete their child’s
		information by email. We do not knowingly collect information from anyone
		under 13. If you believe that we did, email us, and we will delete it.
	</p>

	<h2>Changes</h2>
	<p>
		If this policy changes, we post the new version here and update the date at
		the top. If a change adds a new use or a new recipient of consumer health
		data, or keeps it longer, we ask for your consent again before it applies to
		you.
	</p>

	<h2>Contact</h2>
	<p>
		Skin Groove LLC, Pennsylvania. Email <a href={mailto}>{contactEmail}</a>.
	</p>
</article>
